---Describes a platform-managed, Internet-facing endpoint that routes traffic to a service running inside an instance. Use CreateInstanceRequest.ingresses for ports exposed directly by the instance, including native applications on platforms such as macOS. Use ContainerRequest.export_ports for ports owned by containers. Traffic and TLS boundaries: ``` HTTP [client] --HTTPS------> [Namespace ingress] --HTTP--> [backend] TCP [client] --TLS/mTLS---> [Namespace ingress] --TCP---> [backend] TLS [client] --TLS (routed by SNI, not terminated)------> [backend] ``` Each generated server name routes only to its declared instance and port; no other instance ports are exposed by that ingress. In HTTP and TCP modes, TLS terminates at Namespace and the ingress-to-backend protocol is cleartext HTTP or TCP. TLS passthrough preserves end-to-end encryption: Namespace uses the SNI hostname for routing but does not terminate TLS. HTTP requests require a valid Namespace bearer token with access to the instance by default. HttpMatchRule can explicitly make matching requests unauthenticated. TCP defaults to requiring a Namespace-issued mTLS client certificate with access to the instance; NONE allows any TLS client to connect. In TLS passthrough mode the backend is responsible for server and client authentication.
---@class namespacelabs.compute.Ingress
---@field name? string The name used to generate the Internet-facing server name.
---@field mode? namespacelabs.compute.IngressMode|string The ingress behavior. Must be set.
---@field port? number The port the instance is listening on.
---@field httpMatchRule? namespacelabs.compute.HttpMatchRuleList HTTP routing and authentication rules. Only supported in HTTP mode.
---@field wildcard? boolean Routes all first-level subdomains of the instance wildcard domain to this ingress. Requires the instance wildcard domain to be enabled via experimental.enable_wildcard_domain. Only supported in HTTP mode and mutually exclusive with name.
---@field clientAuthentication? namespacelabs.compute.IngressClientAuthentication|string Configures client authentication in TCP mode. MTLS is incompatible with TLS_PASSTHROUGH, where the backend terminates and authenticates TLS; NONE and UNSPECIFIED have equivalent behavior in passthrough mode. Must not be set in HTTP mode. TCP defaults to requiring mTLS.

---Configures client authentication for TLS-terminating TCP ingress.
---@alias namespacelabs.compute.IngressClientAuthentication "INGRESS_CLIENT_AUTHENTICATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"INGRESS_CLIENT_AUTHENTICATION_NONE"|"INGRESS_CLIENT_AUTHENTICATION_MTLS"

---@alias namespacelabs.compute.IngressList namespacelabs.compute.Ingress[]

---@alias namespacelabs.compute.IngressMode "MODE_UNKNOWN"|"HTTP"|"TCP"|"TLS_PASSTHROUGH"

---@class namespacelabs.compute.IngressRequest
