---@class namespacelabs.compute.VolumeRequest
---@field mountPoint? string The absolute path where the volume is mounted inside the instance.
---@field tag? string A logical identifier for volume reuse across instances. For CACHE volumes, the platform attempts to mount a recently used volume with the same tag. For PERSISTENT volumes, the tag maps to a named durable volume.
---@field sizeMb? string The requested size of the volume in megabytes.
---@field persistencyKind? namespacelabs.compute.VolumeRequestPersistencyKind|string The persistency kind of the volume.
---@field fromSnapshotId? string If set, initializes the volume from the specified snapshot. Only supported for PERSISTENT volumes. If set on a CACHE volume, the request will fail. For persistent volumes, a new snapshot is created starting from the specified snapshot ID.
---@field filesystem? string The filesystem to use for a CACHE volume. Supported values are "ext4" and "xfs" on Linux. If unset, the operating system default is used. XFS requires linux/amd64 and enrollment in the instance.cache_volumes.xfs experiment; requests for XFS are rejected when it is disabled. This field is not supported for PERSISTENT volumes.

---@alias namespacelabs.compute.VolumeRequestList namespacelabs.compute.VolumeRequest[]

---@alias namespacelabs.compute.VolumeRequestPersistencyKind "PERSISTENCY_UNKNOWN"|"PERSISTENT"|"CACHE"

